  "notes": "{溜|た}まる is a godan verb meaning to accumulate, collect, or pile up over time.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{溜|た}める→溜める：02068_tameru⟧ (transitive: to save up, accumulate)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦お{金|かね}→お金：00611_okane⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: money accumulates\n- ⟦{疲|つか}れ→疲れ：03518_tsukare⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: fatigue builds up\n- ⟦ストレス→ストレス：03827_sutoresu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: stress builds up\n- ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: work piles up\n- ⟦{埃|ほこり}→埃：03624_hokori⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: dust collects\n- ⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まる: water pools/collects\n\nUSAGE:\nOften implies gradual, unintentional accumulation, and frequently has a negative connotation (stress, work, fatigue piling up).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {溜|た}まって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: has accumulated / is piled up (resultative state)\n- Note: {溜|た}まる describes the result of gradual accumulation, so the て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form expresses the current built-up state, not an ongoing process. ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"work has piled up\" (there's now a backlog), and ⟦{埃|ほこり}→埃：03624_hokori⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{溜|た}まって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"dust has collected\" (there is dust present now).",
